# ── Data (never committed — see PROJECT_PLAN.md Part 10) ────────────────
# Leading slash anchors to the repo root: an unanchored "data/" also matches
# src/data/, which silently excluded the source package.
# `/data/*` (contents), not `/data/` (the directory): git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so a nested negation under `/data/` can never re-include
# anything. Each level must be unignored in turn.
/data/*
!/data/manifests/
/data/manifests/*
# Subset id lists ARE tracked — §3.9 requires the subsets be reproducible, and
# P1-16 requires every experiment to run on literally the same videos. Git must be
# able to descend into subsets/, so the directory is unignored before its contents.
!/data/manifests/subsets/
/data/manifests/subsets/*
!/data/manifests/subsets/*.txt
!/data/manifests/subsets/*.json
*.npy
*.parquet
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv
*.wav

# ── Model artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# ── Experiment tracking / logs ──────────────────────────────────────────
/logs/
/mlruns/
/experiments/*/*/predictions.parquet
/experiments/*/*/plots/
# Checkpoints and the MLflow store are regenerable; the committed evidence is
# experiments/*/*/{result,history}.json plus reports/*.json, which are small, readable,
# and do not need MLflow installed to inspect.
*.pt
/experiments/mlflow.db
/experiments/mlruns/
# Cached features: 87 MB for 262 clips at two backbones, and fully regenerable from
# committed code plus a committed subset id list (PF-10 explains why they are never
# materialised in bulk).
/data/features/

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Node / frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# ── Source material (not ours to redistribute) ──────────────────────────
docs/*
!docs/README.md

# ── Environment / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# ── Phase 2 generated artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────
# MediaPipe weights: 3.8 MB, re-fetchable and pinned by hash in
# scripts/08_fetch_models.py. Weights are not source.
/models/

# Contact sheets (13 MB) and overlay videos (22 MB) are deterministic outputs of
# committed code plus a committed subset id list -- `make sheets` / `make overlays`
# regenerate them exactly. The evidence that matters (counts, error margins) lives in
# reports/*.md and reports/*_facts.json, which ARE tracked.
/reports/figures/contact_sheets/
/reports/figures/overlays/
